Use the Ford-linked supplier-disruption case as the primary strategic scenario because it explicitly compares alternative mitigation strategies under disruption uncertainty.
The peer-reviewed study was developed in collaboration with Ford and evaluates:
- backup capacity from the primary supplier;
- capacity from a secondary supplier;
- backup inventory;
- disruption probability;
- time to recover;
- response time;
- cost;
- service consequences.
Source:
https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00207543.2021.1975058
The study states that the framework determines the best mitigation strategy and uses strategy graphs to help decision makers choose among alternatives.

This checkpoint produces a major new finding.
Current ServiceNow documentation describes a **Define PO exception mitigation strategy** agentic workflow.
It:
- assesses the material delivery gap;
- locates alternative suppliers with open purchase-order lines;
- recommends order adjustments;
- allows users to review the proposed solution;
- creates an order revision after approval.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/source-to-pay-operations/identify-mitigation-strategies-for-exceptions.html

